<article class="env-lemma" id="0B24">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0B24">Lemma <span data-tag="0B24">5.30.9</span>.</a> The category of topological rings has colimits and colimits commute with the forgetful functor to the category of rings. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The exact same argument as used in the proof of Lemma <a href="/tag/0B21" data-tag="0B21">5.30.6</a> shows existence of colimits. To see the statement on commutation with the forgetful functor to rings we will use Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/0038" data-tag="0038">4.24.5</a>. Indeed, the forgetful functor has a right adjoint, namely the functor which assigns to a ring the corresponding chaotic (or indiscrete) topological ring. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>